These data details the trajectories of 8 surface drifters deployed with drogue during a regular sea survey campaign referred to as BOBLIT2.0.

Buoys used are a set of cylinder-shaped home-made drifters with drogue.

These buoys were equipped with an anchor of 0.5 m long positioned in the water column between 0.8 and 1.3 m depth, allowing them to drift with surface currents. 

Reference time: UTC
